"""The mutations of plan step 7 (the realtime preview node, the audio device layer, the engine's own instances): run with
    python dev/mutation/mutate.py dev/mutation/step7.py
Every one of them should be reported as caught; see mutate.py. (A name starting V is canopy_preview.c, A canopy_audio.c, E canopy_engine.c,
P canopy_package.c, K canopy_install.c, R canopy_registry.c, M canopy_alloc.c.) A mutation that hangs a test is stopped by run_tests.py after
CANOPY_TEST_TIMEOUT seconds (C programs) or 30 s (a Python test): run with CANOPY_TEST_TIMEOUT=60. None of these sends the tests to the machine's
real audio device (a mutation that did would play the tests' signals on it); the ones that choose the backend only choose the null one.
Left out as equivalent: a freed service instance that also reclaims graphs. When a preview's resource is destroyed inside a reclaim, its instance holds
no graph older than the ones that reclaim is freeing (it cannot: those graphs contain the node, so the resource would still be alive), so a second
reclaim inside finds nothing to free."""
V = "src/canopy_preview.c"
A = "src/canopy_audio.c"
E = "src/canopy_engine.c"
P = "src/canopy_package.c"
K = "src/canopy_install.c"
R = "src/canopy_registry.c"
M = "src/canopy_alloc.c"

